    "number": 36568,
    "state": "open",
    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "node: don't throw bad_optional_access on a snapshot network mismatch",
    "user": {
      "login": "Ravan002",
      "id": 95362051,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOBa8cAw",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95362051?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Ravan002",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Ravan002",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Ravan002/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Ravan002/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Ravan002/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Ravan002/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Ravan002/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Ravan002/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Ravan002/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Ravan002/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Ravan002/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "When a snapshot's network magic doesn't match the node's, `SnapshotMetadata::Unserialize` builds an error message with the names of both networks. The node's name comes from `GetNetworkForMagic(m_network_magic).value()`, which is empty on a custom signet because its magic is derived from the challenge and is not one of the built-in ones. `loadtxoutset` with a snapshot made for another network then fails with `bad_optional_access` instead of the message.\n\nThe node side now falls back to \"custom signet\", the only case where the lookup can be empty.\n\n```\nbefore: Unable to parse metadata: bad_optional_access\nafter:  Unable to parse metadata: The network of the snapshot (main) does not match the network of this node (custom signet).\n```\n\nNew unit test `snapshot_metadata_network_mismatch_custom_signet` fails on master with `std::bad_optional_access`. `validation_chainstatemanager_tests` and `feature_assumeutxo.py` pass.\n",
