      "body": "Concept ACK / Approach ACK\r\n\r\nVerified the failure on `master` prior to this patch and confirmed the new test passes with this fix.\r\n\r\nEmpirical Reproduction on `master`\r\nBefore this patch, running `loadtxoutset` on a custom signet node against a mainnet snapshot threw an uncaught `std::bad_optional_access` out of `GetNetworkForMagic(m_network_magic).value()`. \r\n\r\nBecause `loadtxoutset` in `src/rpc/blockchain.cpp` specifically catches `const std::ios_base::failure&`, `std::bad_optional_access` bypassed the deserialization error handler and bubbled up to `CRPCTable::execute` as a generic `RPC_MISC_ERROR` (\"std::bad_optional_access\") rather than the intended `RPC_DESERIALIZATION_ERROR`.\r\n\r\nWhile the fix and the new unit test resolve this issue. I left one small wording suggestion inline.\r\n",
